{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '205,314p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/run/control-request-user.txt | awk '\"'!/''^    (Quote:|Opinion, not verified:)/'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"- e4931 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported control of more than 10 gigawatts of power capacity across its AI hubs as of August 2026.\n- e4932 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported about $103 billion in total contract value.\n- e4933 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale has a $45 billion agreement for Anthropic to use compute resources at its Monarch Compute Campus in West Virginia.\n- e4934 [third_party_view; Billy Duberstein; original source Billy Duberstein 2026-09-18; from gnews:4d4063796374226712c68282 2026-09-18] Motley Fool analyst Billy Duberstein judged that optical connectivity technology would outgrow Nvidia and others in the space over the next few years.\n- e4935 [third_party_view; Kathy Ta, quoted by Billy Duberstein; original source Kathy Ta, Lumentum VP of Investor Relations ; from gnews:4d4063796374226712c68282 2026-09-18] Lumentum VP of Investor Relations Kathy Ta estimated that scale-across and scale-out optical markets were each about 10 times the data-center-interconnect market; initial scale-up CPO was expected from the second half of 2027 at 3–4 times the scale-out market, full optical scale-up at 10 times scale-out, and scale-in at another 10 times.\n- e4936 [third_party_view; Billy Duberstein; original source Billy Duberstein 2026-09-18; from gnews:4d4063796374226712c68282 2026-09-18] Billy Duberstein calculated that Lumentum VP Kathy Ta's bullish scenario of fully optical scale-up would imply 100-fold total addressable market growth, combining 10-fold scale-across and another 10-fold scale-up.\n- e4968 [party_statement; Jim Cramer, quoted by Yahoo Finance from his CNBC remarks; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO 2026-09-17; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said demand for AI-development and inference compute infrastructure was extremely strong and durable; the item attributes the remark to his Mad Money appearance the previous night.\n- e4969 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, quoted by Yahoo Finance from his CNBC remarks; original source Jim Cramer 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Jim Cramer said Broadcom CEO Hock Tan had more orders than almost anybody other than NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang.\n- e4970 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Broadcom 2026-09-02; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom reported that quarterly revenue grew 86% year over year and AI semiconductor revenue grew 221%; the item does not specify the quarter’s end date.\n- e4971 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source Broadcom 2026-09-02; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom’s FY2026 guidance implied 186% annual growth in AI revenue.\n- e4972 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan reaffirmed that Broadcom could generate $115 billion in annual AI chip sales in 2027 and $230 billion in 2028.\n- e4973 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source Broadcom 2026-09-02; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom guided to a 73% gross margin for fiscal Q4, five percentage points below a year earlier, citing a higher mix of XPU sales.\n- e4974 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Yahoo Finance 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Estimates cited by Yahoo Finance suggested that OpenAI and Anthropic could account for 71% of Broadcom’s fiscal 2027 and 2028 XPU deployment.\n- e4975 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Dario Amodei, Anthropic CEO ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei said safety concerns necessitated a slowdown in AI development; the item gives no date or quantified extent.\n- e4976 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI development did not have to slow down; the item gives no date or quantified extent.\n- e4977 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said AI labs with safety concerns should delay product launches until those concerns are resolved rather than advocate a broader slowdown in AI development.\n- e4978 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue doubled to $89 billion in Q2, up 117% year over year.\n- e4980 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Piper Sandler ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Piper Sandler initiated coverage of NVIDIA with an Overweight rating and a $300 price target, citing an estimated 80% share of AI compute and other factors.\n- e4981 [fact; benzinga.com; original source Salesforce ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] Salesforce unveiled Koa, its first Agentforce CRM reasoning model, built on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and running inside Salesforce infrastructure.\n- e4982 [third_party_view; Marc Benioff, speaking on Yahoo Finance's Opening Bid; original source Marc Benioff ; from gnews:499375f1d2854d56642e123d 2026-09-18] Salesforce CEO Marc Benioff said NVIDIA’s business depends on a limited set of customers building enormous data centers.\n- e4983 [fact; Zacks Investment Ideas author; original source Anthropic ; from gnews:64b3da817a58392d7d1677e7 2026-09-18] Anthropic signed a $13.7 billion compute agreement earlier in September 2026.\n- e4984 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI had combined annualized revenue of roughly $100 billion, based on figures circulating in July 2026.\n- e4985 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI need combined annualized revenue of at least $180 billion by the end of 2026 to sustain the AI trade.\n- e4986 [rumour; benzinga.com; original source Unnamed sources cited in the reported figures ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Anthropic's reported annualized revenue run rate reached $65 billion in July 2026, up from $47 billion in May 2026.\n- e4987 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Anthropic's reported $65 billion annualized revenue run rate fell short of investors' roughly $75 billion expectation.\n- e4995 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA generated $164 billion in Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027.\n- e4996 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] The author calculated an annualized Data Center revenue run rate of just under $330 billion from NVIDIA’s first-half FY2027 revenue.\n- e4999 [fact; TechRadar; original source Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA ; from gnews:78a58240705bb94d9382a5dd 2026-09-18] Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA formed the AI Energy Management Alliance to address data-center energy consumption.\n- e5000 [rumour; TechRadar, citing SiliconANGLE; original source SiliconANGLE ; from gnews:78a58240705bb94d9382a5dd 2026-09-18] Anthropic is reported to be planning to join the AI Energy Management Alliance as an additional partner.\n- e5002 [fact; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\n- e5035 [party_statement; NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck, quoted in the article; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck said AgentX benchmark computational demand rose 100-fold on purely numerical tasks; no period was specified.\n- e5036 [party_statement; NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck, quoted in the article; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] Ian Buck said hourly rental rates for NVIDIA A100 instances have risen rather than declined over time, and described demand as remaining robust; no period or rate was specified.\n- e5040 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei announced that its Ascend 960DT would launch as early as Q1 2027, nine months ahead of plan.\n- e5041 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei announced that the Ascend 960PR variant would follow in Q3 2027.\n- e5042 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei said its planned Atlas 960 SuperPoD would link more than 4,000 accelerators via fiber optics to compensate for the Ascend chips’ performance gap with U.S. competitors.\n- e5043 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei said it was not producing enough Ascend chips to meet Chinese demand.\n- e5044 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei outlined plans for Ascend 970 in 2028 and Ascend 980 in 2029, saying each generation would double performance.\n- e5045 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei is open-sourcing its CANN software, which the article says is already compatible with widely used tools such as PyTorch.\n- e5058 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, including $89 billion of Data Center revenue.\n- e5072 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89.0 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 117% year over year.\n- e5097 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale’s prospectus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale said that at the end of August 2026, its in-house data centers hosted 7 MW of active computing capacity and 48 MW operated in leased data-center space, under contracts totaling $2.6 billion.\n- e5098 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale’s prospectus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale said it was preparing 1.3 GW of data-center capacity; the item gives no completion date.\n- e5099 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale’s estimate; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale estimated that its West Virginia data center, under construction, would begin phased commissioning by the end of 2027 and cost about $70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant.\n\n[Themes in force, 9]\n- v10 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's authorities authorize Chinese AI companies to purchase Nvidia H200 chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference sits at rung 2: NVIDIA's Q3 FY2027 guidance assumes no China Data Center compute revenue. That is a sales assumption, not a forecast that Chinese authorities will authorize no purchases. The evidence implies narrow, case-by-case authorization is more likely than no authorization by the\n- v19 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by 2026-12-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-19; reasons: No explicit market consensus or Senate timetable is supplied. The observable reference is that RASA had not passed the Senate as of August 19, which sits at rung 2. The alleged remote-access cases could add pressure for legislation, but the recent evidence reports no Senate action or scheduled vote.\n- v25 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan's Ministry of Economic Affairs introduce performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-28; reasons: The required outcome is formal adoption or entry into force by 2027-01-31, not consultation or consideration. Consultations are confirmed, but the Ministry gave no timeline and the controls were only reported as being weighed. That makes adoption by the deadline less likely than no adoption; the evi\n- v26 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan introduce a criminal ban on AI chip exports to China by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-25; reasons: The status-quo reference is rung 2, and the evidence still makes no ban by the deadline more likely than a ban. Taiwan is considering a criminal ban, and the alleged export case—along with lawmakers’ and experts’ stated view that the law needs to change—adds pressure toward legislation. But the supp\n- v27 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms' access to advanced U.S. chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-25; reasons: The reference is rung 2: the investigation is formally underway and described as likely to remain an ongoing point of contention, with no Commerce deadline or consensus supplied. The access allegations and Taiwanese smuggling enforcement show the issue remains active, but they do not report a Commer\n- v41 (fed-policy-rate, due 2026-09-30) Will the Federal Reserve raise its policy rate at its September 2026 meeting?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-17; reasons: The reference is the fed funds futures market's 86% probability of an increase, which sits at rung 1 (Yes). The later fact says the Federal Reserve raised interest rates on September 17, so the outcome at the meeting is Yes; this is not merely a forecast based on the reference.\n- v43 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-06-30) Will the required U.S. and EU regulatory reviews of NVIDIA's Hugging Face acquisition be cleared by 2027-06-30?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The stated completion plan falls within the deadline and therefore implies clearance by 2027-06-30. The mandatory U.S. filing and The Register's call for intervention add some risk, but neither supplies a regulator's objection, a delay, or a specific reason the reviews will remain uncleared by the d\n- v5 (ai-capex, due 2027-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 4 $700 billion to below $800 billion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is roughly $720–$745 billion for the four companies, which is rung 4. A direct four-hyperscaler estimate of $760 billion and tracking near $745 billion support an implied outcome around $750–$760 billion. Newer estimates of nearly $800 billion refer to the top five, not these fo\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2028-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 4 $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is approximately $1.08 trillion for calendar 2027, which is rung 3. The implied estimate remains about $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate four-to-five share proxy (about $730 billion of $800 billion) to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five est\n\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 3; reasons: The reference is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2. The current evidence implies about $385–390 billion: the first two quarters produced about $164 billion, Q3 Data Center revenue is approximately $100 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and Q4 is estimated at roughly $120–125 billion as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Rubin supply builds. That remains below the $400 billion rung-2 boundary. Strong demand and Rubin orders lift the Q4 estimate modestly, but the 2027–2028 deployment plans are not all FY2027 revenue, and supply availability limits the upside.\n\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,102p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/run/control-request-user.txt | awk '\"'!/''^    (Quote:|Opinion, not verified:)/'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"Thesis v9 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is below $300 billion.\n\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 123 items]\n[Not shown: 1164 more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\n- e74 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in FY2027 Q1, equal to 92% of total sales, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially.\n- e109 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house AI processors, adding competition for NVIDIA’s AI computing products.\n- e127 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus roughly 30% currently, potentially reducing demand for NVIDIA accelerators in China.\n- e153 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting the Bloomberg Intelligence survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese company executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\n- e636 [party_statement; AMD told CNBC; original source AMD ; from gnews:b79717064762299fc9426a13 2026-07-20] AMD said it plans to book tens of billions of dollars in data-center AI revenue starting in 2027, with most of it from Helios.\n- e976 [third_party_view; fool.com author Lyle Daly; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:bdd09874d53aef7b27866d44 2026-07-26] SemiAnalysis forecast that NVIDIA Data Center revenue in the second half of FY2027 would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\n- e2115 [third_party_view; Morningstar; original source Morningstar 2026-08-19; from gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258 2026-08-19] Morningstar estimates NVIDIA Data Center revenue will exceed $300 billion in FY2027 and perhaps $500 billion in FY2028.\n- e2471 [third_party_view; CNBC's Jim Cramer; original source Jim Cramer 2026-08-25; from gnews:1218d24ec31f2081cea0f597 2026-08-25] Jim Cramer said high-bandwidth memory shortages are costing NVIDIA sales; no period or amount was specified.\n- e2510 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Amazon Web Services 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:aws-and-nvidia-to-deliver-2-million-additional-gpus-and-next-generation-infrastructure-for-agentic-and-physical-ai 2026-08-26] AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs across its global infrastructure in 2027–2028.\n- e2517 [fact; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year.\n- e2541 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA began production shipments of Vera Rubin in August 2026 and said it had purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\n- e2562 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's forward outlook included no China Data Center compute revenue.\n- e2567 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected Vera Rubin to account for approximately 20% of Q3 FY2027 Data Center revenue.\n- e2572 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said its available supply supported approximately 70% of expected FY2028 growth, while demand was substantially higher.\n- e2574 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported second-quarter FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra ramp.\n- e2844 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon reported that its custom-chip business exceeded a $25 billion annualized revenue run rate, driven by $225 billion in total commitments from AI labs including Anthropic and OpenAI.\n- e2848 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided to third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, with some revenue expected from Rubin GPUs.\n- e3216 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source fool.com (Daniel Sparks) 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA Data Center revenue rose from 87.9% of total revenue in FY2026 Q2 to 92.5% in FY2027 Q2, increasing each quarter.\n- e3219 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source fool.com (Daniel Sparks) 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that FY2027 Q3 Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion if its share of total revenue stayed at FY2027 Q2's 92.5%.\n- e3222 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA said hyperscale-business growth should reaccelerate in FY2027 Q4 as Vera Rubin supply builds.\n- e3234 [party_statement; Andy Jassy, quoted by fool.com; original source Andy Jassy ; from gnews:6eec748064565c1339694577 2026-08-28] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said Amazon would lack capacity to meet all demand in 2026 and expected that constraint to continue in 2027; he said demand already visible for 2028 was striking.\n- e3805 [third_party_view; theguardian.com; original source theguardian.com 2026-09-03; from gnews:774c4b3a90a519fc0d3c9024 2026-09-03] The Guardian reported that Meta, OpenAI, and Microsoft are developing their own AI chips to reduce reliance on NVIDIA processors, and said this could contribute to slower demand for NVIDIA chips.\n- e3975 [third_party_view; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source Adam Spatacco 2026-09-04; from gnews:bbd72d5fbff98d39746e6cb9 2026-09-04] The author estimated that Vera Rubin could generate close to $20 billion in sales in its first real quarter of shipments.\n- e4052 [party_statement; calcalistech.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] NVIDIA forecast most FY2027 Q3 data-center growth to come from ACIE, with hyperscale growth accelerating in Q4 and through FY2028 as Vera Rubin supply expands.\n- e4185 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:91e29a08de15b30c95cb66ac 2026-09-07] Broadcom raised its forecast for AI chip revenue in the fiscal year ending October 2027 to about $115 billion, from a prior forecast of over $100 billion.\n- e4250 [party_statement; Michael Intrator, quoted by Yahoo Finance; original source Michael Intrator, CoreWeave CEO ; from gnews:f22b97377c3d9832608a0fc8 2026-09-09] CoreWeave CEO Michael Intrator said the company was struggling to meet demand for GPUs and could sell each GPU it had to multiple clients.\n- e4254 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source CoreWeave management ; from gnews:f22b97377c3d9832608a0fc8 2026-09-09] CoreWeave management raised its 2026 total revenue guidance to $12.4 billion–$13.2 billion, citing enterprise GPU-compute demand and a $104 billion total revenue backlog.\n- e4311 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-10; from gnews:ab2afd5299068837dcf8eae0 2026-09-10] Jensen Huang said orders for NVIDIA’s system combining 36 Grace CPUs with 72 Blackwell GPUs were growing 27% month over month.\n- e4330 [party_statement; Benzinga, reporting Oracle CEO Clay Magouyrk's fiscal 2027 first-quarter earnings-call remarks; original source Clay Magouyrk, Oracle CEO ; from gnews:44f4bd6cc91ff33688f1e69f 2026-09-10] Oracle CEO Clay Magouyrk said Oracle had delivered 850 MW of AI capacity containing more than 300,000 GPUs since the end of the previous quarter.\n- e4331 [fact; Benzinga; original source Oracle ; from gnews:44f4bd6cc91ff33688f1e69f 2026-09-10] Oracle closed more than $30 billion in additional AI contracts during its fiscal 2027 first quarter without requiring additional capital; GPU utilization was 97.9%.\n- e4534 [party_statement; fool.com (Manali Pradhan); original source OpenAI ; from gnews:ab387b35d7ed1e8494a84d33 2026-09-12] OpenAI said its Jalapeño chip, co-developed with Broadcom, is intended to run large AI models more efficiently and is planned for deployment across very large data centers; Reuters reported that reducing reliance on NVIDIA GPUs and operating costs was part of the motivation.\n- e4555 [party_statement; Elon Musk, quoted from SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] SpaceX CEO Elon Musk said SpaceX has decided to build exclusively on Nvidia going forward, citing Vera Rubin and its relationship with Nvidia.\n- e4556 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Anthropic and SpaceX ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Anthropic entered into a SpaceX cloud-services agreement worth $1.25 billion per month through 2029 for access to compute across supercomputers featuring roughly 325,000 Nvidia GPUs.\n- e4557 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Google Cloud ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Google Cloud committed $920 million per month through mid-2029 for access to roughly 110,000 Nvidia GPUs, CPUs, memory, and related networking equipment.\n- e4558 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Reflection AI ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Reflection AI signed a multiyear agreement worth up to $6.3 billion to access Nvidia GB300 chips, at a reported $150 million per month.\n- e4562 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Oracle ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] Oracle delivered 850 megawatts of AI capacity containing more than 300,000 GPUs to customers in fiscal Q1 2027, ended August 31.\n- e4563 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Oracle ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] Oracle reported 97.9% utilization across its GPU fleet in fiscal Q1 2027.\n- e4571 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks), reporting Colette Kress's remarks; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA's compute was fully utilized across every cloud it serves.\n- e4572 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks), reporting Colette Kress's remarks; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress estimated revenue opportunity per gigawatt at about 